     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe, so I need you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** Metformin tops out at 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release in adults. That is usually given as 850 mg three times daily. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The ordered dose is about twice the maximum. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total:** for example, 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose:** tell me the dose and frequency you intended.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
